Package: vai-llama-vulkan
Version: 0.0.$(git rev-list --count HEAD)
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: VAI Team <team@vai.example.com>
Installed-Size: 150000
Section: science
Priority: optional
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.31), libstdc++6 (>= 8), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: vulkan-tools
Description: llama-cpp-turboquant Vulkan GPU backend package
 A self-contained Vulkan-based inference engine for large language models.

 This package includes a complete, zero-runtime-dependency installation of
 the llama-cpp-turboquant library with Vulkan GPU acceleration. All required
 runtime libraries are bundled within the package.

 Components:
   - llama-cli: Command-line interface for running LLMs
   - llama-server: REST API server for LLM inference
   - llama-bench: Benchmarking tool for performance testing
   - Tools and utilities for model management

 Requirements (host system):
   - Vulkan driver installed by your graphics hardware vendor
   - No additional runtime packages required - everything is bundled

 Installation location: /opt/vai-llama

 Usage example:
   llama-cli --model path/to/model.gguf --temp 0.7

